WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.250 --> 00:00:05.057
PathProbe 1.2 is out, and it's built for automation.

2
00:00:06.007 --> 00:00:15.881
Add --json to a DHCP run, and Pro streams a live event for every client as it's offered and bound.

3
00:00:16.807 --> 00:00:27.439
On the free tier you still get the final JSON summary, and every run is saved to a run log you can turn off with --no-log.

4
00:00:28.340 --> 00:00:40.409
The new MCP server lets an AI agent run link checks, scans and DHCP tests for you, and read the results as clean JSON.

5
00:00:41.340 --> 00:00:52.495
Save a profile, schedule it every hour, and get an alert on your phone through ntfy, Slack or a webhook when a check fails.

6
00:00:54.107 --> 00:01:02.806
Pull devices straight from NetBox or Nautobot, and check every one with a single command. That one's free.

7
00:01:03.707 --> 00:01:11.256
Common errors now end with a fix line, and pathprobe last repeats your previous command.

8
00:01:12.206 --> 00:01:18.136
And arm64 builds run on a Raspberry Pi, next to Linux and Windows.

9
00:01:18.939 --> 00:01:31.426
Free covers the core tools and five clients. Pro is $9.99, one time, for 1,000 clients, automation, and alerts.

10
00:01:32.639 --> 00:01:37.106
Only test networks you own, or are authorized to test.

11
00:01:37.706 --> 00:01:42.173
Download PathProbe free at getpathprobe.com.
